[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b355e36-38c2-56ac-8348-b3784bc1866b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449616} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f4aaaf-dd54-51ec-8f46-f6472f61e6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b355e36-38c2-56ac-8348-b3784bc1866b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449616} :answer-field/id #uuid "7641d15d-e8d6-5db7-b7ee-7fbcf01436a4" :answer-field/key "$⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450762} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9596a264-1604-5e56-9101-1d727a10926f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449618} {:answer/id #uuid "281f3fd1-7ba1-527c-ae04-c2bd6defe1dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "281f3fd1-7ba1-527c-ae04-c2bd6defe1dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449619} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b2f83df-bcf3-5451-9968-beb33cc6fea5" :answer-field/key "$⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80cfc54f-6519-5a2f-8498-b86f5f3b2228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449620} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e29156-a774-5d52-acbb-563e0b03f2a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80cfc54f-6519-5a2f-8498-b86f5f3b2228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449620} :answer-field/id #uuid "506b6c64-848b-5d2a-a9d9-9c59b4dab9a9" :answer-field/key "$⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "525bde81-7550-5f13-8e28-5c16a04ee9f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-141159" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “$⟨a,b⟩=⟨b,a⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$” is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement “$⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in R$” is true. For any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\overset{―}{\\alpha }=\\alpha .$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$” is false. Notice that if $a=0,$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in R$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Hermitian Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fa21b8e-37bf-549c-a839-8ce08870e48c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449622} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6c92f3-d7f4-5664-9cea-aea62fa675cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b6c92f3-d7f4-5664-9cea-aea62fa675cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449623} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6affe32-9119-5e97-99f7-cd7280f8fef2" :answer-field/key "$⟨ia,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450765} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a053bee-dd05-5cff-aa1d-6027f193cc6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449624} {:answer/id #uuid "db9ce199-be8e-5342-98b1-98b5521bbdb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db9ce199-be8e-5342-98b1-98b5521bbdb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449625} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6da9d5b-43d3-5bf4-b853-80d6034a446d" :answer-field/key "$⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42386a6f-47ee-5149-8998-cff1d0d60579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449626} {:answer/id #uuid "c8170793-2b53-56a5-904e-e65bc454b18f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42386a6f-47ee-5149-8998-cff1d0d60579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449626} :answer-field/id #uuid "096d6ae4-f1ec-5de4-94a5-89d0daa3b32d" :answer-field/key "$⟨ia,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "396a82c3-ba69-5d62-8d39-94fffd303517" :question/math-academy-id "q-141160" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement “$⟨ia,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$” is true.  Indeed, the inner product in ${C}^{n}$ is linear in the first argument. So, a constant multiple from the first argument can be factored out.\n\n- Statement “$⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$” is true. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument and linearity in the first argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\overset{―}{(\\overset{―}{\\alpha })}⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$⟨ia,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$” is false. Notice that $⟨a,a⟩\\in R$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}.$ Therefore, if $a\\ne 0,$ then\n\n$$\n⟨ia,a⟩=i⟨a,a⟩\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$⟨ia,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$”; “$⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=⟨\\alpha a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c0a6001-3780-5910-af1b-80f1dc86bb46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449628} {:answer/id #uuid "711f6d61-9af9-514f-ab7b-3f6b87059a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c0a6001-3780-5910-af1b-80f1dc86bb46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449628} :answer-field/id #uuid "577301d3-bda4-5711-b8ea-c8d7c59e3764" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fd05ec0-7412-5317-bd1f-6fdd48ffae9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449630} {:answer/id #uuid "7e775f74-22c8-5e41-92ca-9b7679c5d763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e775f74-22c8-5e41-92ca-9b7679c5d763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449631} :answer-field/id #uuid "11747fa2-61fa-56a5-ab66-ef191899dff3" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17f12245-1e0f-5cf0-8c20-1a321c65854b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449632} {:answer/id #uuid "2e93e8a1-abd3-5bae-8c25-a6156dc77f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e93e8a1-abd3-5bae-8c25-a6156dc77f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449633} :answer-field/id #uuid "71691d56-9200-5496-becc-0f211d28a39b" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f63719f4-7a1e-5b43-8302-7786de4d0619" :question/math-academy-id "q-141199" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=4=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$ is false. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not invertible” is true. Since $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$ is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is not invertible”; $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f87f060-5b8c-5b4a-806f-8cf93ee4d70d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449634} {:answer/id #uuid "4360a160-1403-523e-8e62-4fbb2ec722d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4360a160-1403-523e-8e62-4fbb2ec722d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449635} :answer-field/id #uuid "359ebe96-94aa-58ea-b60b-be863ac84a52" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb552ac2-1033-5cf0-95e3-c64844f7abfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449636} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cf0040-9b44-519e-ab54-532b2b101a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0cf0040-9b44-519e-ab54-532b2b101a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449637} :answer-field/id #uuid "65159a93-fba0-5a45-abcc-86fe85e1adb6" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39e5820e-dedb-509b-bef8-5b24f4aea7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449638} {:answer/id #uuid "319a4d81-4806-58b2-9a6b-94494e8c5b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39e5820e-dedb-509b-bef8-5b24f4aea7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449638} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8aa8650-12f8-56c0-ac84-85ed73892db0" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dad0d98-37c5-5af9-9c0a-4f0fabec2bcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-141200" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{6} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is true. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$ is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(A)=6$ is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is invertible”; $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083303 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1894719c-d398-515d-9a7b-6af74727106c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Improper Integrals of the Second Kind"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ec25885-aa40-5fcb-b44c-0a2e688c0506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464168} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c96a74-965a-517e-b5f6-459f984a277d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ec25885-aa40-5fcb-b44c-0a2e688c0506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464168} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5903cb9-a0c3-5b7b-8fe9-5fddd4dfc9da" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{3}-8}\\,$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465018} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d929ded6-ebd5-5e24-9347-bc41866b4865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464170} {:answer/id #uuid "d1392ea2-a0cd-532e-a35c-2a7e9db41df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1392ea2-a0cd-532e-a35c-2a7e9db41df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464171} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e25db86-1e25-53ce-99f5-e95966be2e55" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-2}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{3}+8}\\,$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01d2619e-3fff-5c7b-961c-1ea908d7bb9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464172} {:answer/id #uuid "70920143-6447-57e4-9aed-2cba38359928" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01d2619e-3fff-5c7b-961c-1ea908d7bb9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464172} :answer-field/id #uuid "8392c589-f701-5b54-9fbf-943eae559587" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{3}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465020}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a9082ef-b5c5-508a-ad30-c16427769a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141209" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals have finite bounds of integration and an integrand that is unbounded at an endpoint or an interior point of the interval (improper integrals of the second kind on a finite interval)?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{3}-8}\\,$ is not an improper integral since it has finite limits and the function under the integral is finite at every point $x\\in [0,1].$\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{-2}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{3}+8}\\,$ is an improper integral of the second kind since it has finite limits, and \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+8}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to (-2)^{+}.\n$$\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{3}}$ is an improper integral over an *infinite* domain since its lower limit is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{-2}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{3}+8}\\,$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083303 :knowledge-point/