l that apply." :question/worked-solution "The concavity of a function refers to the direction in which its graph curves.\n\n- If the graph curves upward, like a \"smile\" ($⌣$), then the graph is said to be *concave up*.\n\n- If the graph curves downward, like a \"frown\" ($⌢$), then the graph is said to be *concave down*.\n\nIt's helpful to remember the mnemonic \"concave down like a frown.\"\n\nAll graphs I, II, and III curve downward (like a \"frown\") among the given graphs."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f8d9af-560e-5e04-801f-49c3569ea09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464240} {:answer/id #uuid "3683cdbb-cea0-5d3a-88ae-46bbf35523a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07f8d9af-560e-5e04-801f-49c3569ea09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464240} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8b8cb5-e75e-518a-91a0-160dae2c2bc4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bba33a3-e841-5573-8abf-90651ed20a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464242} {:answer/id #uuid "0c34db9f-4df3-5319-9c26-896a5b27e435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bba33a3-e841-5573-8abf-90651ed20a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464242} :answer-field/id #uuid "05d917c1-327f-5ee0-8aed-ef99e81a107b" :answer-field/key "$A$ is  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de2f17c6-86e7-560e-b3af-0ab0f7aab9fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464244} {:answer/id #uuid "06de2a3a-d315-52ff-898b-03d434ea28ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06de2a3a-d315-52ff-898b-03d434ea28ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464245} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bcd47e5-e550-5069-9017-2362f6f7a623" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c320bbb-0961-56b0-99e4-beaa75aa8f10" :question/math-academy-id "q-142358" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\right\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$ is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\right\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is  invertible” is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$ is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4ec697a-de36-58b0-a09b-ffb9c847aeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449652} {:answer/id #uuid "78fdbd67-166e-573c-b77c-2875405073f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4ec697a-de36-58b0-a09b-ffb9c847aeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449652} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4acbd25-fc0e-5df4-a5a0-9e2908a9bffc" :answer-field/key "$\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb540fd1-edb6-5d6c-ba67-f5731cd79a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449654} {:answer/id #uuid "436ef14f-26d4-5b22-b36f-ed6da6246439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb540fd1-edb6-5d6c-ba67-f5731cd79a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449654} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c9e25d7-83f7-5d4a-9ef5-64e221fc60a5" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5d749ec-8e32-58f1-997a-3d7c01f317b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449656} {:answer/id #uuid "93874984-dcb6-5b93-8915-727ca84b807f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93874984-dcb6-5b93-8915-727ca84b807f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449657} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1cc353b-858d-567c-919c-e053dd74f9d8" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4927fd87-c83e-52d3-b9bb-877110a8c514" :question/math-academy-id "q-142474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$ is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)<4$ is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)<4$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d248bbb6-50b4-5d61-a95e-58f318131503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464246} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d0dfe-318f-5100-ac82-83455377b98c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d0dfe-318f-5100-ac82-83455377b98c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d37791a-a285-5a2f-af41-bcd2d8afc075" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3957e353-c39b-5011-af11-d2c9b6787af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464248} {:answer/id #uuid "8a540690-cbd6-5a7b-8e6a-735ce1ef7a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3957e353-c39b-5011-af11-d2c9b6787af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464248} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cfe4de2-b1c4-55bb-a60d-27c7be7257dc" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)<n$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f6788d6-5506-57b7-9972-0d793d0b67f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464250} {:answer/id #uuid "67197e1a-6b46-5a73-9b9e-21d0f7711026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67197e1a-6b46-5a73-9b9e-21d0f7711026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464251} :answer-field/id #uuid "41d8c4a3-f095-50cd-bcf7-92ff6b429b75" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "795129ab-7204-5692-a97c-e32525213e2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-142475" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{n} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, according to the invertible matrix theorem, \n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)<n.$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$*  $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is invertible”; $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a86c9ea-79e9-50fc-bc35-cf2fee7cdfed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} {:answer/id #uuid "8712eb23-d6cb-5de9-b4b0-12bf3d790d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a86c9ea-79e9-50fc-bc35-cf2fee7cdfed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ef167d-4bc6-5f6b-9cd2-3492c740a0f5" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465060} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6eae4da1-dd85-56d5-8efd-a6744dd9efb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} {:answer/id #uuid "915b008a-1011-5090-8324-7e9001f057b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eae4da1-dd85-56d5-8efd-a6744dd9efb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38b7760-7c88-5d50-8e1a-83c437c15443" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "952b73be-fa27-5c33-ac51-fe0f11cb7be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464256} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc948d7-8345-54f5-aac4-3efcd42070c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fc948d7-8345-54f5-aac4-3efcd42070c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6398a3-5006-54e1-b7af-c62ec5fc9eea" :answer-field/key "$A$ has $8$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7036dc73-9ca4-59f2-b983-11eaacfb5a4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142476" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{8} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times$  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has $8$ pivot columns” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c2659df-70b4-5256-87fa-2a34198af876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449658} {:answer/id #uuid "77a2cd60-bf16-5a97-b3a5-f6ed36dd706c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77a2cd60-bf16-5a97-b3a5-f6ed36dd706c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449659} :answer-field/id #uuid "3592b310-da06-5773-8430-cf897b63efce" :answer-field/key "$A$ is  **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450783} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71487a84-b41a-585b-8ff3-f6fbfac9393d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449660} {:answer/id #uuid "dc36f444-1255-5d82-87f6-8355261ee483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc36f444-1255-5d82-87f6-8355261ee483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449661} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d161315-6d73-5e59-8ca0-0d5fd8273d52" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0d44763-7df9-5816-b934-fe067cf8d583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449662} {:answer/id #uuid "3786226d-53c4-521c-afec-80c21f875609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0d44763-7df9-5816-b934-fe067cf8d583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449662} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c5e784e-a241-51f7-84ca-848b80cea623" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a4ded73-dd50-5431-9dd3-a7f4831d94c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-142544" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix which has only $3$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=7=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is  **not** invertible” is true. Since $A$ has $n=7$ columns and $3$ of them is a non-pivot one, it follows that    \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Col}(A))=7-3=4\\ne 7.\n$$\n\n Thus,  according to the invertible matrix theorem $A$ is  **not** an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$” is true.  Indeed, since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=\\text{rank}(A)=4$,  then $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$ is false. Since $n=7$, according to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =7-4 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is  **not** invertible”; “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7674d21-f661-53ce-9c89-cda7d267f9a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464258} {:answer/id #uuid "d066aa6a-00c3-5f23-98dd-319579643453" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d066aa6a-00c3-5f23-98dd-319579643453" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464259} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c9a6ba0-7305-59d6-bbfa-58571090472e" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465063} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de9a03d7-7939-515f-8654-2f2de5034c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464260} {:answer/id #uuid "7f550a9c-d6f4-5c67-9f0d-97820488e12a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de9a03d7-7939-515f-8654-2f2de5034c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464260} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7ce5955-9552-5cc1-8f40-54a9de65a9b1" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465064} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3476d2b-a50b-5168-93b9-9c079b1c3e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464262} {:answer/id #uuid "47cf8085-adf4-5988-ba4e-585371322b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47cf8085-adf4-5988-ba4e-585371322b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464263} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fdce47d-a87d-56b0-9930-397fb4a161b0" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6378e369-5031-5af4-8366-576c75d82fa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-143001" :question/problem "![](images/67/67706db50684aef52269d20065caa21e4301834835e10e1fd3e456646ae2b32e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{DF}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} & =(\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB})+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FB}-\\overset{\\to }{DB} & =\\overset{\\to }{FB}+\\overset{\\to }{BD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FD} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} & =\\overset{\\to }{DF}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BF}$; $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd858e4-c107-59b8-8e32-c58f003a163e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464264} {:answer/id #uuid "82cab609-ba28-56b3-86af-ebf0fe1e4d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cd858e4-c107-59b8-8e32-c58f003a163e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464264} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc024899-46d7-5349-9838-e39e86f76569" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465066} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc2e7d3-82e2-531b-bf65-d7814c7dd00d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464266} {:answer/id #uuid "84d7dd87-f0a4-554a-83c1-5e294d1f7592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84d7dd87-f0a4-554a-83c1-5e294d1f7592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464267} :answer-field/id #uuid "606ac01f-e466-55e0-acee-aa5b70d8fe3a" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e897c19c-be3d-51f0-9c09-3ddea644c0f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464268} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd00f67-28d3-5d1e-9797-5e9edb8eb8a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e897c19c-be3d-51f0-9c09-3ddea644c0f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464268} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d8d9975-f6a8-50c8-9aa0-5883d4b25f10" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32cdac5a-ca17-59c1-8641-8b3b47e09944" :question/math-academy-id "q-143006" :question/problem "![](images/15/15f4bd7f8ecf8f61ce84858e33cdfa468b0de360fac19b0713b6b2dbc4af8d2e.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$ is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}-\\overset{\\to }{AF} & =\\overset{\\to }{AB}+\\overset{\\to }{FA} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$ is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+(\\overset{\\to }{EA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{DB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD}=\\overset{\\to }{CB}$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BE}-\\overset{\\to }{DE}-\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BE}+\\overset{\\to }{ED})+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}+\\overset{\\to }{DC} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BC} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{CB}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\overset{\\to }{DE}+\\overset{\\to }{EA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}=\\overset{\\to }{DB}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275114 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99c0be41-4842-5d84-9243-b20970ca65f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464270} {:answer/id #uuid "ad3a1711-1ce6-584c-8666-fd81316fdd9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad3a1711-1ce6-584c-8666-fd81316fdd9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464271} :answer-field/id #uuid "19e8b9f1-2710-5c4d-97d6-670c3ce72f83" :answer-field/key "$P(X=2,Y=1)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6dc7de0-fb70-572e-9395-bf45e4359ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464272} {:answer/id #uuid "3e54788f-563d-5897-822c-4ffcb07e00ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e54788f-563d-5897-822c-4ffcb07e00ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464273} :answer-field/id #uuid "a82999e5-03fb-56c4-8ba2-aa587b618145" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465070} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63a65e48-8a48-5658-be41-145c5aab2fa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464274} {:answer/id #uuid "3d42055b-43bb-5621-bee4-f237edcf65e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d42055b-43bb-5621-bee4-f237edcf65e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464275} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d508279-cf49-5ea0-a9cb-97c308df61f8" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a347e7c2-3db8-5058-926f-eeec20d91744" :question/math-academy-id "q-143331" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.6$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.6$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.75$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=2,Y=1)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=2,Y=1)=f(2,1)=0.15.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.2\\cdot 0.75=0.15.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =0.6=0.8\\cdot 0.75={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,2) & =0.2=0.8\\cdot 0.25={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(2,2) & =0.05=0.2\\cdot 0.25={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is true. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=2,Y=1)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=1)$; “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$”; “$X$ and $Y$ are independent”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05112f38-a021-5475-adbd-e2dab978dcc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464276} {:answer/id #uuid "f1e27b73-a786-50ad-befd-9af1bceb49a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05112f38-a021-5475-adbd-e2dab978dcc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464276} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd056097-b408-58b6-9d07-0013368a4eac" :answer-field/key "$P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2dc0905-947a-5502-afb0-e31f99420f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464278} {:answer/id #uuid "11f19573-031c-5a4e-92e5-69affffb8f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2dc0905-947a-5502-afb0-e31f99420f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464278} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1c916fa-571a-52d8-9c46-9dc13d9b2bdd" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd7ef690-8b54-58fe-9a21-0a4293d10ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464280} {:answer/id #uuid "4edd5db2-ceaa-577d-84c0-e2e7014339d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd7ef690-8b54-58fe-9a21-0a4293d10ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464280} :answer-field/id #uuid "793fa71c-2507-582d-aece-7b85ad9d5350" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e48e8cd-fab9-56d8-9673-3c5737feeff5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143333" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=2,Y=2)=f(2,2)=0.4.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.5\\cdot 0.6=0.3.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=2,Y=2)\\ne P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275116 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e75e0302-d864-58b2-85e3-94ee824dd2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464282} {:answer/id #uuid "81aa670d-7b50-5dbc-876a-7211f2efdce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e75e0302-d864-58b2-85e3-94ee824dd2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464282} :answer-field/id #uuid "849d37e5-d949-564c-9ffb-269b4790643f" :answer-field/key "$P(X=0,Y=3)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465075} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a48738c-0702-53e5-be01-701b938eac9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464284} {:answer/id #uuid "ab470c08-52aa-55f5-9185-42801db2ff25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a48738c-0702-53e5-be01-701b938eac9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464284} :answer-field/id #uuid "0576c586-45c4-5fc2-ac45-e4e7ee3e0065" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc1e965d-3466-5f79-8631-71934ff94795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464286} {:answer/id #uuid "21ff56fe-204e-548f-804b-20588bc44e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc1e965d-3466-5f79-8631-71934ff94795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464286} :answer-field/id #uuid "51cb2efc-d508-5ae6-a259-fc9980908d16" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16b71f57-df8c-5727-afc2-cdadae9185c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143334" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ | $0.75$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=0,Y=3)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=3)=f(0,3)=0.15.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(3)=0.25\\cdot 0.3=0.075.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=3)\\ne P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd7e9f64-cbbd-5bbd-8464-3f61b6f11586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464288} {:answer/id #uuid "b46bc96b-ac7e-5f3f-a9a5-4cdfc8aba11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b46bc96b-ac7e-5f3f-a9a5-4cdfc8aba11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464289} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca347041-dadc-56e2-bbf1-f6ebc4c70e09" :answer-field/key "$P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e699ac2-764b-512c-8f0d-5172d00686da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464290} {:answer/id #uuid "006bf10f-88fe-5637-949f-4aa29407bc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e699ac2-764b-512c-8f0d-5172d00686da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464290} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f7c971-351f-53ff-be7e-c7304f5c86bf" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17db8ae0-64d6-5514-9124-5fa3d5e8dba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464292} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a98f0c-64a9-57fe-b332-0fefcb246690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17db8ae0-64d6-5514-9124-5fa3d5e8dba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464292} :answer-field/id #uuid "da33b576-bcf0-5c09-83dd-58d6caaeb72b" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "743eb09d-bf29-57ce-b05b-46da6dccd3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143338" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.16$ | $0.01$ | $0.03$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.64$ | $0.09$ | $0.07$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.16$ | $0.01$ | $0.03$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.64$ | $0.09$ | $0.07$ | $0.8$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.8$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=3,Y=2)=f(3,2)=0.64.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.8\\cdot 0.8=0.64.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,2) & =0.16=0.2\\cdot 0.8={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,4) & =0.01\\ne 0.2\\cdot 0.1={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(4) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2775cce0-304f-5113-963a-e28a11e24992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464294} {:answer/id #uuid "128d1ceb-39cf-5da3-8419-5a7d8a02044d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2775cce0-304f-5113-963a-e28a11e24992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464294} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d189a29-6c25-5569-854b-c13fc0526360" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad3a30bf-90ea-5614-8226-e124a25c10b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464296} {:answer/id #uuid "b3343df9-8a4a-5259-9ba0-3cd40ddbf9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad3a30bf-90ea-5614-8226-e124a25c10b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464296} :answer-field/id #uuid "af0ced41-0208-507d-b83f-0b656205df0e" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb8af9ea-b637-5ed4-b6ba-f9ad08c1f112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464298} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0da6fb-3bb6-55a5-a319-72bfe95326c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb8af9ea-b637-5ed4-b6ba-f9ad08c1f112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464298} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee63d585-1abb-575b-b286-f0fc73957802" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d571385e-cc3b-5950-8471-24ba60f93b53" :question/math-academy-id "q-143435" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.35$ | $0.65$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=1)=f(1,1)=0.05.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.3\\cdot 0.65=0.195.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=1,Y=1)\\ne P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d0391e2-c7ef-5a32-a6e4-a1dd2f23ab04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449664} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6ce1e9-a2d9-513e-9218-2fe7d1e0a8a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d0391e2-c7ef-5a32-a6e4-a1dd2f23ab04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449664} :answer-field/id #uuid "0aed2ada-8cf1-5887-add8-5891a536ebb4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450786} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af8c890-adc0-5501-b776-d23219000bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449666} {:answer/id #uuid "78ea7642-4a88-5dd4-9c0e-b9cddd5255a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1af8c890-adc0-5501-b776-d23219000bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449666} :answer-field/id #uuid "e11f78a0-08ce-50e3-88fc-e1011761342e" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "634c8a5c-c46d-507d-a2df-cc1a7726c974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449668} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3e28a0-079e-52e9-9123-05a2f2341769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d3e28a0-079e-52e9-9123-05a2f2341769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449669} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6e79aa7-abeb-5d53-9e24-d52f8f63b70a" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5342a760-4f6b-57f7-989c-35eadd9600b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-143533" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R\\right\\}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{3} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=3=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$  \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R\\right\\}=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\,\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=3,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =3 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=2\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement $det(A)=0$ is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible we must have   $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $det(A)=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161979 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "691d2386-08e0-5e84-8528-ca09e15fee56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464300} {:answer/id #uuid "40fc8e5d-a7c6-5dee-ad15-ced14c3143c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40fc8e5d-a7c6-5dee-ad15-ced14c3143c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464301} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe6f4042-36ad-5790-9b6a-ec08b4a4e1de" :answer-field/key "$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 11 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465084} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a166b78e-fbfa-54cb-b123-2bd64adb1d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464302} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf7898e-f1aa-583f-936b-db61e1a09fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaf7898e-f1aa-583f-936b-db61e1a09fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464303} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d8b8c80-ca14-520f-b6c2-4799187a9aeb" :answer-field/key "$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465085} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d54f34b-efcc-5076-9803-a07b0f77a6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464304} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf8d2b6-60b1-5f51-852c-b6a4df097275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d54f34b-efcc-5076-9803-a07b0f77a6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464304} :answer-field/id #uuid "671893c7-dec8-5832-a276-3876dd47a359" :answer-field/key "$R=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2475e8ae-4517-52f5-bd41-fe3d91352945" :question/math-academy-id "q-143680" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${r}_{12}\\ne {r}_{21},$ we obtain $R\\ne {R}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77834ff3-1b22-5a38-b89b-f82d5ab71856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449670} {:answer/id #uuid "9b29bb6e-dcf9-528a-a29e-2d6d71349d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b29bb6e-dcf9-528a-a29e-2d6d71349d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449671} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9da5bec-12d7-5de8-b874-3910e58e4788" :answer-field/key "If $A$ is a square matrix, then $A+{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450789} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e310a01-b5b6-5b95-8ec3-f1d8a5a533b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449672} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0b9210-7a27-56eb-aa08-e1bd408b372d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa0b9210-7a27-56eb-aa08-e1bd408b372d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449673} :answer-field/id #uuid "56acf37f-34e4-5d10-a6c2-3e5a5d140e65" :answer-field/key "If $A$ is a symmetric matrix, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5b9fcc-8b52-530c-9210-d313e83c7a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449674} {:answer/id #uuid "df70da07-5141-53a7-a1ee-97990272f70b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c5b9fcc-8b52-530c-9210-d313e83c7a0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449674} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6dbf8d-010e-5415-bfc1-dbb221779069" :answer-field/key "The sum of two $n\\times n$ matrices is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df88ef9d-a81d-55a1-b088-252f805046b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-143685" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “If $A$ is a square matrix, then $A+{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric” is true. Indeed, for any square matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+{A}^{T})^{T} & ={A}^{T}+({A}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}+A \\\\  & =A+{A}^{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $A$ is a symmetric matrix, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)” is true. Indeed, for any non-singular symmetric matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{-1})^{T} & =({A}^{T})^{-1} \\\\  & ={A}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The sum of two $n\\times n$ matrices is always symmetric” is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrices \n\n$\\,$ $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nHowever, their sum is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $A$ is a square matrix, then $A+{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric”; “If $A$ is a symmetric matrix, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d290cf67-6df4-50a4-a125-89a4d83e9229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449676} {:answer/id #uuid "7a88fac1-3096-5661-afa0-47f72ffc8f65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a88fac1-3096-5661-afa0-47f72ffc8f65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449677} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d1092b5-ba66-50b4-8bee-d42517f8ecdf" :answer-field/key "The product of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450792} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01dc726f-0a06-5fe8-a402-62bb327452b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449678} {:answer/id #uuid "9b7f8d67-7b14-52c5-b5e2-ee93081a984b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01dc726f-0a06-5fe8-a402-62bb327452b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449678} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b21dbc2-c542-5c91-8cc5-fb3798ea6bc5" :answer-field/key "If $A$ is *any* $n\\times n$ matrix, then $A+{A}^{2}$ is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b0c6601-486b-5c49-ae54-f084a8b9d18c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449680} {:answer/id #uuid "491b7869-9458-5892-a187-1e25f2d50b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491b7869-9458-5892-a187-1e25f2d50b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449681} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f0701ff-8dbe-5272-b976-e1595f15b3ee" :answer-field/key "If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then $A{A}^{T}-{A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "416a1d82-1004-5007-b882-19d5aaa3af4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-143686" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The product of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric” is true. Indeed, for any diagonal matrices $A$ and $B,$ their product $AB$ is also diagonal, and any diagonal matrix is symmetric.\n\n- Statement “If $A$ is *any* $n\\times n$ matrix, then $A+{A}^{2}$ is always symmetric” is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nHowever, $A+{A}^{2}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+{A}^{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then $A{A}^{T}-{A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric” is true. Indeed, for any square matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A{A}^{T}-{A}^{T}A)^{T} & =(A{A}^{T})^{T}-({A}^{T}A)^{T} \\\\  & =({A}^{T})^{T}{A}^{T}-{A}^{T}({A}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & =A{A}^{T}-{A}^{T}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The product of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric”; “If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then $A{A}^{T}-{A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb77d39b-75ff-5747-b99c-9cd47f41c51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449682} {:answer/id #uuid "94345635-817a-5aa4-a7a2-498d963121ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94345635-817a-5aa4-a7a2-498d963121ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449683} :answer-field/id #uuid "eaedc8bd-f59e-5871-bfc5-e7553143409e" :answer-field/key "The sum of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0f84e81-499d-55d4-ac5e-99eb38720728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449684} {:answer/id #uuid "79aeba54-2cd8-5240-8cb3-d19dcfbe4680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0f84e81-499d-55d4-ac5e-99eb38720728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449684} :answer-field/id #uuid "a09ef516-6c8d-5da1-b76b-438fb19a83e7" :answer-field/key "If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$  matrix, then $A-{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bcbb1cb-2004-5967-bedb-dae9a7275c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449686} {:answer/id #uuid "2bda30dd-367b-5982-ba71-617e5ac2752d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bcbb1cb-2004-5967-bedb-dae9a7275c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449686} :answer-field/id #uuid "06250cb3-b876-5df2-a845-d13c4b38939b" :answer-field/key "The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "62cdcd34-c338-59e0-b65d-2d882ff231e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-143687" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The sum of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric” is true. Indeed, for any diagonal matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$  matrix, then $A-{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric” is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nHowever, $A-{A}^{T}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-{A}^{T} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric” is false. As a counterexample, consider the symmetric matrices \n\n$\\,$ $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nHowever, their product is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The sum of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Properties of Symmetric Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c7b2a77-1693-52b5-938e-64e6e1f2ceab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449688} {:answer/id #uuid "d01fdf31-92a5-57b3-8671-eed1b16afb81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d01fdf31-92a5-57b3-8671-eed1b16afb81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449689} :answer-field/id #uuid "e94131fa-ce78-5678-be60-13aa8ed6ef76" :answer-field/key "If $A$ is symmetric, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450798} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8381806-836c-50a9-93cd-2a9d74f5530d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449690} {:answer/id #uuid "0d643587-3414-5f09-b4a1-16711a9473e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d643587-3414-5f09-b4a1-16711a9473e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449691} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e188018-640d-552b-b4ec-5b8295f202cc" :answer-field/key "The sum of *any* two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450799} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f537b5-ef33-531d-bfd8-f1876dac11f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449692} {:answer/id #uuid "8087e2ff-5cd7-5646-a803-00c97f657498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8087e2ff-5cd7-5646-a803-00c97f657498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449693} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0930087-8fb8-5b80-8794-d9766c9702be" :answer-field/key "If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "812925c4-9b82-5457-b638-58a29d609de3" :question/math-academy-id "q-143688" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “If $A$ is symmetric, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)” is true. Indeed, for any non-singular symmetric matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{-1})^{T} & =({A}^{T})^{-1} \\\\  & ={A}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The sum of *any* two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric” is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric” is true. Indeed, for any $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{T}A)^{T} & ={A}^{T}({A}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $A$ is symmetric, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)”; “The sum of *any* two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric”; “If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162063 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6b40e85-685d-5aab-a444-8d6308f092ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464306} {:answer/id #uuid "f496eb60-ea3c-5012-94d5-6a88a7ee132b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f496eb60-ea3c-5012-94d5-6a88a7ee132b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464307} :answer-field/id #uuid "62d3db58-a8e1-53d5-9263-64aabffee523" :answer-field/key "$0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465087} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ad996b1-ee92-58c1-945e-288e24a1684a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464308} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1b11cb-7840-58b1-9605-17c342ec821e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f1b11cb-7840-58b1-9605-17c342ec821e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464309} :answer-field/id #uuid "09e8be2c-6838-5976-a996-7c966f243d0e" :answer-field/key "${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465088} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c589b14-4ce2-5a9d-99dd-9f8e826f588a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464310} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b7057b-4aee-5f4a-8fde-1b87c3a33f06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7b7057b-4aee-5f4a-8fde-1b87c3a33f06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464311} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d636b7d-f826-57af-9dce-2dff4230118a" :answer-field/key "$f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62d0b863-0ebd-5fe2-bf2e-b910931d25fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-143865" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check the given conditions:\n\n- Condition “$0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$” is true. Every value of $f(x,y)$ in the table satisfies $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$ is true. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =0.4+0.3+0.2+0.1=1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition “$f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function” is true. Because $f(x,y)$ satisfies conditions “$0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$” and ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$, it is a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$”; ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$; “$f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275142 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162063 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af749281-56f2-5884-a556-cb423dd42d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464312} {:answer/id #uuid "3864aedc-5b81-5741-9865-3d9d09d081c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218646431