wer-field/id #uuid "7fe8e435-6a97-5600-ab65-5a06ed47e374" :answer-field/key "$f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b48a6d92-bb8d-5520-9846-8b67d6784e46" :question/math-academy-id "q-143869" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.16$ | $-0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.24$ | $0.35$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check the given conditions:\n\n- Condition “$0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$” is false. The value of $f(2,2)$ in the table does not satisfy $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$ is true. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =0.2+0.15+0.16-0.1+0.24+0.35=1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition “$f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function” is false. Because $f(x,y)$ does not satisfy condition “$0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$”, it is *not* a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b3ae7d4-993f-5430-b747-8986186d90fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464336} {:answer/id #uuid "2869d7f3-1b96-5dd5-b0ee-6c3483909fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2869d7f3-1b96-5dd5-b0ee-6c3483909fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464337} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4fe13b9-b461-5404-b579-d68d54cca664" :answer-field/key "The point $(8,-16)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc53e1ca-d2b5-5bf5-9f01-959fdb70deba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464338} {:answer/id #uuid "161f0366-48c8-5ba7-af35-ca8c9a24aa9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "161f0366-48c8-5ba7-af35-ca8c9a24aa9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464339} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f506c58-26c9-5596-a8a5-1dd2c2a8a692" :answer-field/key "The point $(-6,12)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d21af34-3afd-5f67-97ee-02ead5548978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464340} {:answer/id #uuid "95080681-e8e2-5196-9852-abd8418b6244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d21af34-3afd-5f67-97ee-02ead5548978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464340} :answer-field/id #uuid "06baf51a-09b9-58c1-8af9-5d0f7258e947" :answer-field/key "The point $(8,16)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d122f7d-248a-5adb-b7f8-d6731998c545" :question/math-academy-id "q-147666" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,3)$, $(-2,0)$ and $(2,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 6 & 12 & -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-3,6)$, $(-6,12)$ and $(8,-16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(8,-16)$”; “The point $(-6,12)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1dc097f-1d45-5954-ab58-ae2d5d480624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464342} {:answer/id #uuid "7baca676-28e5-5fc3-a177-996e1ce40ce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7baca676-28e5-5fc3-a177-996e1ce40ce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464343} :answer-field/id #uuid "85b6b509-5bca-5a90-a4c2-4fce1e466596" :answer-field/key "The point $(-1,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "949bf759-caef-5f6e-8122-5b8ee2d18f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464344} {:answer/id #uuid "7359df24-8e1b-527f-88c9-aa439b96a42c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "949bf759-caef-5f6e-8122-5b8ee2d18f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464344} :answer-field/id #uuid "f82e39bc-0ba9-546e-8634-7c85456024dd" :answer-field/key "The point $(-3,12)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bc8121f-bbec-513b-a049-d0ed40f6ee68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464346} {:answer/id #uuid "1ada007f-92c5-599a-97cf-02ed61244306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bc8121f-bbec-513b-a049-d0ed40f6ee68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464346} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d54219b-bc8a-5314-ba61-2881e9c259be" :answer-field/key "The point $(7,-12)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1bd0a07c-db54-5589-8d88-4cb094a8efc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-147667" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,-1)$, $(1,0)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$ \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 12 & 2 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,12)$, $(-1,2)$ and $(7,-14).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(-1,2)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04ca492-480a-5623-adc9-4e521cf13ef9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464348} {:answer/id #uuid "4b47