 17592186464353} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8ee657-f121-51ff-9eea-9d96b2041f94" :answer-field/key "The point $(2,-4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84cfa7aa-4b60-5511-b592-0b61d5c3575c" :question/math-academy-id "q-147668" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,0)$, $(0,-3)$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 12 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -24 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-4)$, $(12,-24)$ and $(-8,16).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(12,-24)$”; “The point $(2,-4)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275182 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd338836-3b2b-5b26-8e4d-99852c2a9bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464