value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464358} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fa4186b-ca78-58e7-a4f0-491a35712d01" :answer-field/key "The point $(18,-3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84f6bd2a-70dc-5d03-9a24-101d7db5f112" :question/math-academy-id "q-147669" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,3),(0,-2),$ and $(4,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -6 & -5 \\\\ -33 & 18 & 15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(11,-33)$, $(-6,18)$ and $(-5,15).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(-5,15)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef5f574-e5ac-53d5-88f0-491f23791c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1759