 :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464365} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0dc0749-8a7d-54bf-bd14-a1ab81456b68" :answer-field/key "The point $(12,-24)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "097bf1b0-31a1-5f77-a025-cb53554e53aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-147670" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,1),(0,0)$ and $(2,2)$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$  \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 0 & -6 \\\\ -24 & 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are  $(12,-24),(0,0)$ and $(-6,12).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(12,-24)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19f788cf-dc8b-5b55-ade8-a9c81ce81890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/r