ext} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464371} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a0e2e3f-7761-580b-bf82-de8d40eb59b4" :answer-field/key "The point $(8,-16)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32f22262-a81f-543c-b306-489aa3da6008" :question/math-academy-id "q-147671" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,-1),(0,2),$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 12 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(8,-16),$ $(-6,12)$, and $(7,-14).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The point $(7,-14)$”; “The point $(8,-16)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc36f534-6b27-5619-a29e-9954d0310adb" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Continuity of Two-Piece Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf01e8d5-4816-5120-a96e-31a559b63b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/re