trix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $EF=FE={I}_{3}.$ Computing $EF$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EF & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $FE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FE & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $EF=FE={I}_{3}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $FG=GF={I}_{3}.$ Computing $FG$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FG & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $FG=GF={I}_{3}$ is false. As a result, $F\\ne {G}^{-1}$ and statement $F={G}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $EF=FE={I}_{3}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d3c794-0fd5-59cf-aa3b-e2dc7aaf04de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464402} {:answer/id #uuid "13f3080f-2a2e-5f68-ad93-0dc5cf51e7c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32d3c794-0fd5-59cf-aa3b-e2dc7aaf04de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464402} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd59685b-e36e-57fc-b0de-87a808e2950e" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465135} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3a5d282-29ec-5062-816b-49f4eab07dc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464404} {:answer/id #uuid "058f6b84-807f-5c96-abd5-f5b7e248e1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "058f6b84-807f-5c96-abd5-f5b7e248e1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464405} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f03e31d-0bb7-55ed-a6f4-3f59148d1089" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465136} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba0d7311-7b93-5e4b-a814-aa12d234796a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464406} {:answer/id #uuid "45d3662e-9e38-5c21-9f50-1fdddab0e3a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45d3662e-9e38-5c21-9f50-1fdddab0e3a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464407} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a145f94-84f0-55f4-9b95-b1c537573877" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08ceb92c-03d7-50b0-a12d-3ba81bdd7b99" :question/math-academy-id "q-150011" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d2aa60719643235f5ae684d59607199731626e15bac40fd6b14d071c099ab4a.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/2b/2b8ef08638551571caa43150080a8550a0b61ed24eaa7c6da73fe66edd161e8e.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/28/28db5c349d3455c58f81da7c181586ba4e0ad5662f35faa2575d6622b3713988.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$; ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6861910f-6d1e-51d4-89aa-e94ccdc1daef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464408} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff3e9d8-9224-590f-a556-21e0f19a6cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6861910f-6d1e-51d4-89aa-e94ccdc1daef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464408} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2d825a4-6901-57a2-9930-5d754820d8f2" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3073e19f-2806-5672-b534-cfe2db245ac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464410} {:answer/id #uuid "090dcb5c-5958-5538-8b54-75141969de9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "090dcb5c-5958-5538-8b54-75141969de9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464411} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6c59f83-3272-51a6-b5bb-233286cf4fae" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465139} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f071eee-8c41-5a00-9649-943ecfb7e8f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464412} {:answer/id #uuid "0d3e4fef-b214-5bad-bd98-71272ba97893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f071eee-8c41-5a00-9649-943ecfb7e8f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464412} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe47fa17-0302-5990-92cb-7f28cb8bce17" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a5b0685-d096-5d41-9e82-0f5600340c35" :question/math-academy-id "q-150018" :question/problem "![](images/67/678ab825415e107bca9554d90e2ad5a4d8cc90a5ef68d817972ef98dfc165922.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/0e/0e8d0fcf619987f49869cc6ae9eb5cb0c7acbbb23f45ce8f64626dfd1debdc63.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$ is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/b2/b2bec1f1da172b623f20d28fd0e9c5a248cf00dc621769851ca33b3b545b8592.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Continuity at a Point Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b31e43b-f648-5104-87eb-9773f3ab646e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464414} {:answer/id #uuid "3d35c8cd-77d0-53cc-a4cc-aced0894a8ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d35c8cd-77d0-53cc-a4cc-aced0894a8ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464415} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b8a13fa-9617-54e3-bbe2-6955813e1a61" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f4a8985-f129-51ee-90ba-f275667cf211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464416} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee3e448-a245-5b5f-b945-6fed6ab9ba8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ee3e448-a245-5b5f-b945-6fed6ab9ba8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464417} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ecbc8bf-447d-5cfb-910a-1731abb7fcb4" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465142} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f641b6b9-8e1f-56a9-8045-25fba6743213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464418} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a83a00-2862-5236-a123-0fff57a9c078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f641b6b9-8e1f-56a9-8045-25fba6743213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464418} :answer-field/id #uuid "d00037b3-4d1d-5237-ab02-131d4a0e9d8f" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=f(0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34e01e01-4068-57dc-b51d-390e4a966eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464420} {:answer/id #uuid "6f80b835-5186-5fa4-8ff2-00fb3050a5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e01e01-4068-57dc-b51d-390e4a966eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464420} :answer-field/id #uuid "d812efd5-93ef-587c-91ab-5168f29affce" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "234c8730-7a9e-5554-ac25-1a6863fd17a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-152913" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x<0 \\\\ 0, & x=0 \\\\ {e}^{-x}, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$” is true. Using the expression for the middle branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists” is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(x+1) \\\\  & =(0)+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=0$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=1\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=f(0)$ is false. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=1\\ne f(0).$  $\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$” is false. Since not all statements “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$”; “${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists”; ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=f(0)$ are true, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$”; “${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Continuity at a Point Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36bce25c-ae20-59d1-9043-9dbcfea9a802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449700} {:answer/id #uuid "6a4361ac-431f-547a-803e-4a0b7c9e817c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a4361ac-431f-547a-803e-4a0b7c9e817c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449701} :answer-field/id #uuid "831bf201-4eb6-50e7-9162-050f0f497dfd" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450804} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12332b96-561d-5286-8d56-a7fc1c7dcdc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449702} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bea772-0212-5add-a1da-cfc603fd711f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12332b96-561d-5286-8d56-a7fc1c7dcdc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449702} :answer-field/id #uuid "e968dce4-01bc-5e94-9ec8-2ad947e888d9" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)$ exists" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f155f2a5-3221-5204-a95d-da113933ae51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449704} {:answer/id #uuid "bf93800f-f5c2-5ee1-ae44-edd362ecacd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f155f2a5-3221-5204-a95d-da113933ae51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449704} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e0dbc21-d10e-5f56-a69b-a3dd306e953b" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)=f(-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf95d85f-fbe0-5382-a889-038fe9f60d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449706} {:answer/id #uuid "d75daa7d-7469-508d-afed-e5814954a39a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf95d85f-fbe0-5382-a889-038fe9f60d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449706} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bfe78b2-2139-5859-b4b6-c62f3fee23e5" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc9788c2-4a6c-53d6-898a-18877d069efc" :question/math-academy-id "q-152925" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3-x}, & x\\le -1 \\\\ x+1, & x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$” is true. Using the expression for the first branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(-1)=\\sqrt{3-(-1)}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)$ exists” is false. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}(\\sqrt{3-x}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3-(-1)} \\\\  & =2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}(x+1) \\\\  & =(-1)+1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{-}}f(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {(-1)}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=-1$ does not exist. $\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)=f(-1)$ is false since the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=-1$ does not exist. $\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$” is false. Since not all statements “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$”; “${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)$ exists”; ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}f(x)=f(-1)$ are true, the function $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8edb0a6c-f22f-56cf-9545-2fae93896db2" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Continuity at a Point Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:ans